# Git commit authorship

When creating git commits:

- Do **not** add `Co-Authored-By`, `Signed-off-by`, or any trailer that names Cursor, Copilot, Claude, or other AI tools
- Do **not** mention Cursor, AI, or an assistant in the commit message body or subject
- Commit messages should read as authored solely by the human user
- Use only the message content the user requested (or a normal project-style message); no attribution footnotes

```text
# ❌ BAD
feat: add health hook

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# ✅ GOOD
feat: add health hook
```
